1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,506
This revision brings the chamber, gun, pumps, gauges and gas connection into one assembly.

2
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:10,539
The chamber remains two hundred by two hundred by three hundred millimetres internally.

3
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:18,175
We have retained the simpler pumping arrangement: chamber to turbo, then through a flexible foreline to one mechanical backing pump.

4
00:00:18,175 --> 00:00:23,092
There is no separate roughing bypass or high vacuum isolation valve in this revision.

5
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:30,150
The gas supply model ends at the six millimetre push fitting; the regulator and cylinder remain outside this design scope.

6
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:35,828
The front door opens without moving the gun or any rear service connection.

7
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:40,563
The clear opening is one hundred and eighty by two hundred and seventy millimetres.

8
00:00:40,563 --> 00:00:42,901
The viewport opening is seventy diameter.

9
00:00:42,901 --> 00:00:46,894
Both pressure gauges and the mass flow controller connect at the rear.

10
00:00:46,894 --> 00:00:53,454
The left wall remains blank, while the two spare right side K F twenty five ports now have removable blanking caps.

11
00:00:53,454 --> 00:00:59,900
Next, the integrated close up shows how the gun compression fitting attaches and how its cap sets the gun height.

12
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,606
There are two different connections here.

13
00:01:03,606 --> 00:01:07,712
The K F clamp joins the compression fitting to the welded chamber flange.

14
00:01:07,712 --> 00:01:12,944
The threaded cap at the top has a different job: it compresses an O ring around the gun tube.

15
00:01:12,944 --> 00:01:18,794
I have replaced the single solid placeholder with a separate body, threaded cap, follower and tube seal.

16
00:01:18,794 --> 00:01:24,250
The detailed thread and seal seat are illustrative, pending the actual purchased fitting drawing.

17
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:30,761
First, the fitting body sits on the chamber K F flange, with the face seal between them.

18
00:01:30,761 --> 00:01:34,255
This face seal is separate from the O ring around the tube.

19
00:01:34,255 --> 00:01:38,519
The body is lowered into place, while the compression cap remains loose.

20
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:42,250
We are showing the mechanical assembly with the chamber vented.

21
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:46,859
The two clamp jaws close around the mating flange rims.

22
00:01:46,859 --> 00:01:49,447
Tightening the wing nut secures this joint.

23
00:01:49,447 --> 00:01:52,395
From now on, the body stays fixed to the chamber.

24
00:01:52,395 --> 00:01:55,885
You do not loosen this K F clamp to adjust the gun height.

25
00:01:55,885 --> 00:01:59,917
Height adjustment happens at the separate threaded compression cap.

26
00:02:01,217 --> 00:02:06,238
With the upper cap loose, feed the gun service tube upward from inside the chamber.

27
00:02:06,238 --> 00:02:07,812
The gun head stays inside.

28
00:02:07,812 --> 00:02:12,047
The twenty five point four millimetre tube slides through the fitting.

29
00:02:12,047 --> 00:02:17,250
This animation follows the existing gun geometry; the roof and body remain stationary.

30
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:23,536
Now move the complete gun up or down to choose the target to substrate distance.

31
00:02:23,536 --> 00:02:29,331
In our chamber model, the working range is seventy five to one hundred and fifty millimetres.

32
00:02:29,331 --> 00:02:31,201
Here we return to one hundred.

33
00:02:31,201 --> 00:02:33,320
The body and K F clamp stay still.

34
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,750
Support the gun while the cap is loose.

35
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:42,093
Hold the tube at the selected position and turn the cap clockwise, viewed from above.

36
00:02:42,093 --> 00:02:44,348
The cap advances down the body thread.

37
00:02:44,348 --> 00:02:49,450
Its shoulder pushes the follower onto the O ring, squeezing the seal against the tube.

38
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:51,705
The tube does not rotate with the cap.

39
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:58,350
The model uses an illustrative two millimetre thread pitch, so two turns produce four millimetres of cap travel.

40
00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:03,333
That is an animation dimension, not a tightening instruction for the purchased part.

41
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,794
The section view shows the load path.

42
00:03:06,794 --> 00:03:11,408
The moving cap shoulder presses the follower, which compresses the tube O ring.

43
00:03:11,408 --> 00:03:14,503
The lower face seal and K F clamp remain undisturbed.

44
00:03:14,503 --> 00:03:20,577
O ring deformation is shown schematically to explain the mechanism; it is not a seal stress calculation.

45
00:03:20,577 --> 00:03:25,833
The actual mating flange and centering ring must also have enough clear bore for the tube.

46
00:03:27,133 --> 00:03:33,529
Inside the chamber, the ninety diameter substrate stage is six millimetres thick, with its top at height forty.

47
00:03:33,529 --> 00:03:38,370
The one millimetre reference substrate puts the actual working surface at forty one.

48
00:03:38,370 --> 00:03:45,458
The target to substrate distance is adjustable from seventy five to one hundred and fifty, with one hundred as the default.

49
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:47,820
The bent shutter is one millimetre sheet.

50
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:51,854
Its flat midplanes are separated by two hundred and forty millimetres.

51
00:03:51,854 --> 00:03:56,464
The lower blade underside is at fifty three, exactly twelve above the substrate.

52
00:03:56,464 --> 00:03:59,230
It rotates eighty degrees to uncover the sample.

53
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:05,108
These are the same nominal dimensions and checked motion envelope established in the chamber revision.

54
00:04:06,508 --> 00:04:14,071
The turbo exterior is reconstructed from the Edwards E X T seventy dimension drawing, rather than from an invented pump shape.

55
00:04:14,071 --> 00:04:22,114
Its I S O sixty three flange is ninety five diameter, and the reference overall height is one hundred and fifty seven point zero five.

56
00:04:22,114 --> 00:04:27,996
Four double claw clamps join the pump flange to the chamber flange, with a face seal between them.

57
00:04:27,996 --> 00:04:30,397
The chamber is carried by its own stand.

58
00:04:30,397 --> 00:04:40,061
The standard E X T seventy manual specifies a K F sixteen backing outlet, so this model includes a K F sixteen to K F twenty five adapter for the requested hose.

59
00:04:40,061 --> 00:04:44,983
If your actual pump has a K F twenty five outlet variant, that adapter is omitted.

60
00:04:46,383 --> 00:04:52,129
The mechanical pump is an Edwards R V three reference, imported from the supplier's actual STEP file.

61
00:04:52,129 --> 00:04:55,030
It is a layout reference, not a confirmed purchase.

62
00:04:55,030 --> 00:05:00,776
The flexible K F twenty five hose connects the turbo backing outlet to the rotary pump suction inlet.

63
00:05:00,776 --> 00:05:06,977
This distinction matters: the other rotary pump port is its exhaust and is not connected back to the chamber.

64
00:05:06,977 --> 00:05:11,983
The hose routing is modeled as a curved core with corrugations and separate end flanges.

65
00:05:11,983 --> 00:05:16,819
The selected commercial hose must accommodate that route and its minimum bend radius.

66
00:05:16,819 --> 00:05:20,858
The blue moving markers illustrate the gas path, not a flow simulation.

67
00:05:22,258 --> 00:05:25,695
The two lower rear ports carry the Pirani and Penning gauges.

68
00:05:25,695 --> 00:05:30,879
Their chamber port centres are at height ninety, fifty millimetres to either side of centre.

69
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:32,794
Both use K F twenty five fittings.

70
00:05:32,794 --> 00:05:39,668
Each gauge is mounted behind a ninety degree elbow so its sensing opening does not look directly at the sputtering target.

71
00:05:39,668 --> 00:05:45,753
The housings and connectors are reference geometry because the actual gauge model numbers were not supplied.

72
00:05:45,753 --> 00:05:52,233
Their final mounting orientation, temperature and magnetic field clearances must follow the selected gauge manuals.

73
00:05:53,633 --> 00:05:58,995
The upper rear port is the mass flow controller connection, at height two hundred and ten.

74
00:05:58,995 --> 00:06:06,919
A K F twenty five to female quarter inch V C R adapter connects to the controller's male V C R outlet, with a metal face seal gasket.

75
00:06:06,919 --> 00:06:10,435
Both controller ports are assumed male V C R, as requested.

76
00:06:10,435 --> 00:06:18,716
The reference body follows the H O R I B A E four forty J layout, including a one hundred and twenty four millimetre face to face distance.

77
00:06:18,716 --> 00:06:24,615
A rear shelf supports the controller independently so its weight is not carried by the gas fitting.

78
00:06:24,615 --> 00:06:29,858
The signal connector is shown on top; its electrical cable is outside the present model.

79
00:06:31,258 --> 00:06:37,272
On the supply side, the male V C R inlet meets a female V C R adapter assembly and its metal gasket.

80
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:40,820
The other end of that adapter is quarter inch female N P T.

81
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:46,773
Into it screws the quarter inch male N P T push fitting for six millimetre outside diameter tubing.

82
00:06:46,773 --> 00:06:50,562
This is the same adapter chain recovered from the earlier chat.

83
00:06:50,562 --> 00:06:55,193
V C R seals at the gasket face; N P T is a separate tapered thread interface.

84
00:06:55,193 --> 00:06:59,462
The exploded view separates those parts so their functions are visible.

85
00:06:59,462 --> 00:07:05,055
Gas would enter at the push fitting, pass through the controller, and then enter the chamber.

86
00:07:05,055 --> 00:07:08,483
The model stops at the push socket, exactly as requested.

87
00:07:09,883 --> 00:07:21,729
The delivered CAD includes complete and loading states, the refined compression fitting, the turbo connection, the backing pump and hose, both gauges, and the complete mass flow controller adapter chain.

88
00:07:21,729 --> 00:07:30,366
The R V three is supplier CAD; the turbo is a dimension drawing reconstruction; gauge bodies and several fitting details remain reference envelopes.

89
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:36,319
The supplier pump STEP has a pre existing topology issue and is retained as visual reference geometry.

90
00:07:36,319 --> 00:07:43,789
This is a much more complete mechanical layout, but not a fabrication release or a claim of a fully engineered operating system.

91
00:07:43,789 --> 00:07:50,733
Pressure strength, seals, purchased interfaces, cooling, electrical controls and interlocks still require verification.
